  <diagram id="agentdecompile-recovery-pipeline" name="AgentDecompile — the recovery pipeline, end to end">
    <mxGraphModel dx="0" dy="0" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="4400" pageHeight="2936" background="#16181c" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <UserObject label="" description="Reading order: header and key, then the main pipeline left to right from stage 0 (open, add or resume) through stage 8 (whole-image byte identity), then concurrent lanes A–E, bounded resolution ladders A–F, ownership locks, the failover rule, the export target and the full legend. Solid arrows are prerequisites, dashed arrows are failover or labelled feedback, and every gate must pass before its claim is accepted. Candidates, compiled code, local parity zeros, runtime calls and original bytes never count as recovered source or whole-image proof; only whole-file hash equality is terminal. Design only: future checks are not run; agentdecompile-recovery-pipeline.outline.md is the text outline with the same node ids." id="0"><mxCell/></UserObject>
