        <UserObject label="" tooltip="AgentDecompile — the recovery pipeline, end to end&#10;&#10;In the app: `?node=overview-header`&#10;&#10;Text outline of agentdecompile-recovery-pipeline.svg; the primary accessible reading form of that diagram. Each anchor equals the node id in `pipeline-model.json`, the `&lt;g id&gt;` in the SVG and the object id in the `.drawio` file, whose single link per object points back to this anchor. &quot;In the app&quot; gives each node's location in the workbench, which resolves it against the active project. Symbols that carry meaning are spelled out in words.&#10;&#10;Summary: Reading order: header and key, then the main pipeline left to right from stage 0 (open, add or resume) through stage 8 (whole-image byte identity), then concurrent lanes A to E, bounded resolution ladders A to F, ownership locks, the failover rule, the export target and the full legend. Solid arrows are prerequisites, dashed arrows are failover or labelled feedback, and every gate must pass before its claim is accepted. Candidates, compiled code, local parity zeros, runtime calls and original bytes never count as recovered source or whole-image proof; only whole-file hash equality is terminal. Design only: future checks are not run; agentdecompile-recovery-pipeline.outline.md is the text outline with the same node ids.&#10;&#10;Reading order: named stages retain prerequisites; evidence feeds back and verification starts early. Every card answers: what we're trying to do, how, what goes in and comes out, what gates it.&#10;&#10;Design target: recover from the…" link="agentdecompile-recovery-pipeline.outline.md#overview-header" id="overview-header"><mxCell style="group" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="L1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="20.5" width="1651" height="111.88" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject>
        <mxCell id="c3" value="AgentDecompile — the recovery pipeline, end to end" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=nowrap;overflow=visible;fontFamily=DejaVu Sans;fontSize=30;fontColor=#f2f4f7;fontStyle=1;spacing=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingRight=0;spacingTop=0;spacingBottom=0;" vertex="1" parent="overview-header"><mxGeometry x="0" y="0" width="906" height="42" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c4" value="Reading order: named stages retain prerequisites; evidence feeds back and verification starts early. Every card answers: what we're trying to do · how · what goes in and comes out · what gates it." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=nowrap;overflow=visible;fontFamily=DejaVu Sans;fontSize=14;fontColor=#98a0ad;spacing=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingRight=0;spacingTop=0;spacingBottom=0;" vertex="1" parent="overview-header"><mxGeometry x="0" y="48.8" width="1542.64" height="19.6" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c5" value="Design target: recover from the best evidence, reuse only what transfers, verify at the level of use — packs, generated bindings, headers and readiness reports with explicit capability limits." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=nowrap;overflow=visible;fontFamily=DejaVu Sans;fontSize=14;fontColor=#f0c060;fontStyle=2;spacing=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingRight=0;spacingTop=0;spacingBottom=0;" vertex="1" parent="overview-header"><mxGeometry x="0" y="72.8" width="1511.28" height="19.6" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c6" value="Runs on a laptop; scales by concurrency, then by donated idle compute and free cloud nodes; task-specific budgets and isolated storage probes; complete prepared inputs enable independent continuation; see execution-contracts companion." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=nowrap;overflow=visible;fontFamily=DejaVu Sans;fontSize=12.5;fontColor=#98a0ad;fontStyle=2;spacing=0;spacingLeft=0;spacingRight=0;spacingTop=0;spacingBottom=0;" vertex="1" parent="overview-header"><mxGeometry x="0" y="94.38" width="1651" height="17.5" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <UserObject label="" tooltip="How to read this in 20 seconds&#10;&#10;In the app: `?node=how-to-read`&#10;&#10;1. Follow prerequisites; identity/calibration iterate and parity runs continuously.&#10;2. Lanes may overlap within ownership, resource and snapshot-dependency limits.&#10;3. Try applicable lookups; exports state capabilities, uncertainty and evidence.&#10;&#10;Key: solid arrow = dependency, dashed red arrow = failover, feedback = dashed arrow back to an earlier stage, G diamond = gate, padlock = one owner, uppercase header word = family, full legend at the bottom." link="agentdecompile-recovery-pipeline.outline.md#how-to-read" id="how-to-read"><mxCell style="group" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="L1"><mxGeometry x="2700" y="22" width="1660" height="112" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject>
