        <UserObject label="" tooltip="Stage 4: C/C++ candidates&#10;&#10;In the app: `?node=stage-4`&#10;&#10;- Family: source recovery (SOURCE RECOVERY)&#10;- Catalog verbs (consolidated plan §2.1): `corpus.ghidra-bulk`&#10;- Tag: isolated mutable outputs / PDB / Wine state&#10;- Trying to: Produce readable candidates; preserve the floor until replacement acceptance passes.&#10;- How:&#10;  - recovery unit is not compilation unit is not comparison unit&#10;  - compile pass then candidate (real_c is compile-only)&#10;  - fail then deterministic helpers (sanitizer/preparse) then retry then ONE bounded LLM cleanup then retry then keep asm&#10;  - never repeat valid unchanged work&#10;  - repair explains preserved machine behavior&#10;- In to out:&#10;  - in: scaffold + decompiler output&#10;  - out: compiled candidates + scoped compile receipts&#10;- Gate: compile admits candidate, not replacement. In the app: `?node=gate-4`&#10;- Failover loop (dashed, below stage 4): when compile fails, run helpers, then one bounded LLM cleanup, then retry; failover never blocks sibling work. In the app: `?node=stage-4-failover`" link="agentdecompile-recovery-pipeline.outline.md#stage-4" id="stage-4"><mxCell style="group" vertex="1" connectable="0" parent="L2"><mxGeometry x="1704.28" y="200" width="523.44" height="425.68" as="geometry"/></mxCell></UserObject>
